(7809479, 1303957, 8759, '<td valign="top">
It''s the short name for the ex Socialist Republic of Romania: Oficiul Național De Turism Carpați - National Office for Tourism Carpathian.
<br/>
<br/>This is a gift from friend but I do remember having a similar one when I was a small boy. Quite neat.
<br/>
<br/>The ONT Carpați toy bus is a legendary piece of Romanian toy history, manufactured by the Metalogobus Factory in Bucharest between the 1960s and 1980s. 
<br/>Key Details:
<br/>Manufacturer: Metaloglobus Bucharest.
<br/>Material: It is a friction-powered tin toy made primarily of metal with plastic or rubber wheels.
<br/>Branding: Labeled "ONT Carpați" after the Oficiul Național de Turism (National Tourism Office), which used similar full-sized coaches during the communist era.
<br/>Collectibility: These are now considered rare vintage items. Depending on their condition and original packaging, they can be found on collector sites<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2026-02-09 07:17:24.</i></td>', 'It''s the short name for the ex Socialist Republic of Romania: Oficiul Național De Turism Carpați - National Office for Tourism Carpathian.

This is a gift from friend but I do remember having a similar one when I was a small boy. Quite neat.

The ONT Carpați toy bus is a legendary piece of Romanian toy history, manufactured by the Metalogobus Factory in Bucharest between the 1960s and 1980s. 
Key Details:
Manufacturer: Metaloglobus Bucharest.
Material: It is a friction-powered tin toy made primarily of metal with plastic or rubber wheels.
Branding: Labeled "ONT Carpați" after the Oficiul Național de Turism (National Tourism Office), which used similar full-sized coaches during the communist era.
Collectibility: These are now considered rare vintage items. Depending on their condition and original packaging, they can be found on collector sites', '2026-02-09 07:15:47.000000', '2026-02-09 07:17:24.000000', 0),
